The classic vanilla Rogue kill is E-grave then back toss for up to 5d30 
plus whatever the daggers themselves did.

In Spork the E-grave is no longer 100% and the atomic backtoss is gone, 
but Magicbane still puts the scare into a lot of monsters.

When untwoweaponing was a zero time action the Rogue could score a 
Magicbane scare, along with the offhand damage and then (thanks to 
speed) do a Magicbane backstab before the target had a chance to flee.

As a Magicbane backstab is up to +d30, even a silver saber barely beats 
this and only for a few targets, almost none of which will be on Astral.

A shield of reflection frees up the amulet slot for power/life plus 
allows the use of a wider dragon scale selection.

I'm still leaning towards twoweapon for the other classes that can use 
it (Rangers?), but the atomic backstab is so good that I'd rather apply 
the skill slots elsewhere.

It's a pity because spork rogues now start with knife and dagger skills 
and Crysknife does more damage to everything on Astral than the saber. 
(Especially when thrown as a last ditch defense.)

So my rut is still flee to Sokoban, use my infinitely reusable starting 
pile of ascendable weapons to kill things hiding behind boulders then 
use reflection to survive long enough to dunk nymph juice for lamp 
polish to get Magicbane.  (If only I had an elven rogue, just for the 
weapons...  I might even be tempted to finish with +7 robe and shield)

